	(global_label "GND"
		(shape bidirectional)
		(at 580.39 403.86 0)
		(fields_autoplaced yes)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left))
		(uuid "2a0003a0-68dd-51d3-aa3d-eedfe3c27672")
	)
	(text "GAIN PLAN, WORKED FORWARD -- source ceiling to ADC full scale. A range change re-fires\nthis arithmetic; that is the point of writing it here rather than in a note file.\n\n  ADC full scale = 0.56 x (VREFH - VREFL) = 0.56 x 5 V = 2.80 Vpp diff = 0.990 Vrms\n  INA1650 gain   = 1 V/V EXACTLY -- there is no gain to share between stages, so the\n                   attenuator does ALL the range work in BOTH modes.\n\n  Rtop = 10k per leg, Rbot = 9.09k per leg, Rspk = 332R per leg (switched by K1-K4)\n  LINE    (Rbot alone):        2.00 Vrms in -> 0.943 Vrms  (95.3% of FS)\n  SPEAKER (Rbot || Rspk):      30.0 Vrms in -> 0.931 Vrms  (94.0% of FS)\n  Zin, line mode, differential = 2 x (Rtop + Rbot) = 38 kOhm  vs the >= 20 kOhm decree\n\nNOTE WHAT IS *NOT* HERE: no gain stage. That is a consequence, not an omission -- the\nINA1650 is fixed at 1 V/V, so any topology that attenuated further would need one, and\nevery extra stage multiplies the attenuator's own noise before the ADC sees it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 650.24 39.37 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "02401dba-6334-5f03-999b-a79754fc0777")
	)
	(text "F9 AS AN INEQUALITY, NOT A PARTS PREFERENCE -- and the mechanism is NOT the divider ratio.\n\nThe INA1650's CMRR is trimmed against its OWN internal 500 kOhm resistor network. Whatever\nsource impedance the attenuator presents lands IN SERIES with those internal resistors, so\nit is the IMBALANCE between the P and N legs -- not the absolute value, not the ratio --\nthat detunes the trim. The ceiling is roughly:\n        CMRR_limit  ~  20 x log10( 500 kOhm / dRs )\n  dRs = 500 Ohm  -> 60 dB      dRs = 50 Ohm -> 80 dB      dRs = 5 Ohm -> 100 dB\n  S12 acceptance is CMRR >= 60 dB, so dRs must stay BELOW ~500 Ohm to clear it at all,\n  and below ~50 Ohm to clear it with the margin an acceptance line deserves.\n\nRtop is 10k. 50 Ohm of imbalance on 10k is 0.05 % -- so DISCRETE 0.1 % SINGLES DO NOT\nCOMFORTABLY CLEAR IT, and 1 % parts miss it outright. THE ARRAY RECOMMENDATION FALLS OUT\nOF THIS INEQUALITY rather than preceding it:\n  * Use INTEGRATED RESISTOR ARRAYS for Rtop and Rbot -- P and N legs in ONE package.\n  * The spec that matters is RATIO MATCHING and TRACKING, not absolute tolerance.\n  * TEMPCO TRACKING is the half that discrete 0.1 % parts cannot buy at any price: the\n    decree is -20 to +70 degC, a 90 degC span, and two discrete parts with independent\n    +/-25 ppm/degC drift 2250 ppm apart across it -- 0.225 %, which is 4.5x the 0.05 %\n    budget above. CMRR measured at 25 degC on the bench would pass and then degrade in\n    a hot car. An array's elements share a die and track.\n  * K1-K4 are TWO-POLE relays switching both legs together for the same reason: two\n    single-pole parts have independent contact resistance and would imbalance Rspk.\n\nThis is why F8 put the divider AHEAD of the switch and why F9 is a BOM requirement."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 650.24 170.18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "33807463-a95c-50d6-a23b-33f1af7baaf5")
	)
	(text "WHY THE RANGE ELEMENT IS A RELAY, DERIVED -- not asserted (Q2 convention).\n\nAt the 30 Vrms speaker ceiling the INPUT NODE sees +/-42 V peak. Walk the options:\n  * Analog switch AT THE INPUT: needs rails containing +/-42 V. The largest analog rail\n    on this board is +/-13V5_A. IT DOES NOT CONTAIN THE SWING. Excluded by arithmetic,\n    which is exactly the reasoning that made F8 say 'or use a relay'.\n  * Analog switch AFTER a fixed first-stage attenuator: the switch then sees ~1 Vrms in\n    NORMAL use -- but the misconfiguration case is not exotic, it is the DEFAULT user\n    error: speaker level applied while the board still thinks it is in line mode. The\n    node then sits at 30/2.02 = 14.2 Vrms = +/-20 V peak, and the switch is across it.\n    Survivable only by adding clamps that then load the signal.\n  * RELAY in the bottom leg: contacts are indifferent to +/-42 V, add no distortion\n    (S6.2's own preference), and the misconfiguration case is a non-event.\n  -> RELAY. K1-K4, two Form A poles each, shorting Rspk to ground on BOTH legs together.\n\nFAIL DIRECTION IS DELIBERATE: de-energised = LINE (Rbot alone, less attenuation). The\nopposite choice -- de-energised = speaker -- is the better FAIL-SAFE, since the safe state\nis maximum attenuation, and it was rejected on power: line is the common install, so it\nwould energise four coils continuously in the ordinary case, ~120 mA on +5V_D forever.\nTHE CONSEQUENCE, STATED: a coil or driver failure in a speaker-level install presents as\n14.2 Vrms into the INA1650, which CLIPS but does not damage it (500 kOhm inputs and the\n1k/1W series parts limit the current). Audible distortion, not silence and not smoke.\nREOPEN if a field failure makes that the wrong trade.\n\nREF A / REF B (12, 9) are tied to AGND_REF, a QUIET GROUND REFERENCE, through a 0R --\nthe banked disposition: 'must be driven from a low impedance, NOT left to a divider.'\nA BUFFERED MID-RAIL IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* USED: the INA1650 runs on +/-13V5_A, so its\nown mid-rail IS ground, and a buffer would only add a noise source and a failure mode\nbetween the reference pin and the thing it references. VMID_OUT is tied back to VMID_IN\nthrough 0R with a noise-reduction cap, which is the datasheet's own arrangement.\nThe 0R positions exist so a star point can be moved at layout WITHOUT a schematic edit."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 650.24 330.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "b6a7f1f5-d4cf-560b-9ecb-443cb01f791f")
	)
	(text "SIGNAL-SENSE, ESD, AND THE OUTSIDE WORLD.\n\nSIGNAL-SENSE MUST NOT CHATTER. S6.1 sets ~10 mVrms, resistor-settable. Music AT the\nthreshold is not a steady tone -- it crosses in and out on every phrase, so a bare\ncomparator would square-wave the remote-out logic and click the amplifiers on and off.\nTWO things are therefore required and NEITHER is optional:\n  * HYSTERESIS: assert at ~10 mVrms, release at ~5 mVrms (6 dB), so the release point is\n    a different signal level, not a different sample of the same one.\n  * ASYMMETRIC TIME CONSTANTS: attack ~50 ms (fast enough not to clip the first note),\n    release ~20-30 s (long enough to ride a track gap, a quiet passage, or a fade).\n    The release constant is the one that matters and it is LONG -- it is set by the\n    longest musical silence the user will tolerate as 'still on', not by electronics.\n  * THE SENSE PATH TAPS *AFTER* THE ATTENUATOR, at ATTn_*, so it inherits the range\n    switching and can never see the 30 Vrms it is monitoring. Tapping the raw input --\n    the obvious place -- would put +/-42 V on a comparator input.\n  SIGNAL_SENSE lands on the expander (U43 P0 as an input), NOT a native GPIO, because\n  03_control has none left. Detection latency over I2C is irrelevant at a 20 s release.\n\nSERIES PROTECTION IS SIZED FOR AN AMPLIFIER FAULT, NOT NORMAL DRIVE. The 1k/1W parts\nahead of every divider assume a shorted output stage parks a full rail on the pin: at\n42 V across 1k that is 1.8 W momentarily and 42 mA into the network -- the resistor is\nthe fuse, and it is specified at 1 W so it survives long enough to be the thing that\nfails safely rather than the INA1650.\n\nESD MUST NOT BUY ITS PROTECTION WITH DISTORTION. Any diode across an audio node is a\nvoltage-variable capacitance in the signal path. Requirements for this position:\n  * LOW capacitance (< 5 pF) and, more importantly, FLAT capacitance vs voltage.\n  * BIASED OUTSIDE THE SIGNAL RANGE -- referenced to +/-13V5_A, not to ground, so the\n    junctions never modulate across the audio swing. A ground-referenced clamp sits at\n    its most nonlinear exactly where the signal lives.\n  * S12's CCIF twin-tone criterion is the test that SEES this, and it is the same\n    mechanism the mute shunt's off-capacitance was called out for -- second instance,\n    same measurement.\n  Part not yet pinned: this is an F38 line, and it wants manufacturer stated (F38a).\n\nRCA SHIELDS land on the S9 chassis star through the RC network, on 09_io -- NOT here,\nand NOT to AGND_REF. Named so the two are not confused at layout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 650.24 500.38 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "fecbd97a-c8a9-57d2-9a9c-8bc11dd3fae0")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
